# JavaScript Bundle Rebuilding

This project uses bundled JavaScript files for production. After editing ANY of the source JS files listed in the globs above, you MUST rebuild the bundles.

## How to Rebuild

Run this command from the project root:

```bash
cd /Users/khoi/Desktop/TEMP/_Personal/_Cursor/_DandDy && python3 scripts/simple_bundle.py
```

## Bundle Outputs

- `manager.bundle.js` - Used by `index.html` (Character Manager)
- `builder.bundle.js` - Used by `builder.html` (Character Builder)

## IMPORTANT

- **Always rebuild after editing source files** - The bundles are what actually run in production
- **Never edit the bundle files directly** - They are auto-generated and will be overwritten
- **Verify the rebuild succeeded** - Check for "Wrote bundle:" messages in output

## Source Files → Bundles

**manager.bundle.js** includes:
- app-*.js files
- version.js, demo-characters.js
- data-*.js files
- builder-config.js, builder-dnd-data.js, builder-utils.js, builder-narrators.js, builder-services.js, builder-components.js

**builder.bundle.js** includes:
- app-config.js, app-auth.js, app-character-mapper.js, app-storage.js, app-api.js, app-character-sheet.js, app-portraits.js
- data-*.js files
- All builder-*.js files
